  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add a stored writable Title to StoredSession.</step>
    <step order="2">Generate a 3–6 word grounded title at first substantive exchange with the specified fallback chain.</step>
    <step order="3">Add PATCH /api/ai/chat/sessions/{id} (title) returning 404 on missing, 204 on success.</step>
    <step order="4">Add unit tests (title-gen fallback + rename persists + 404).</step>
    <step order="5">dotnet build + publish size.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a stored Title conflicts with the read-computed Title used by the recent-sessions projection, STOP and escalate rather than silently double-sourcing titles.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>No stored title; BuildSessionTitle:811 is read-computed only.</existing>
    <extension>No writable field exists — must add Title to StoredSession + a rename endpoint.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Generated titles have nowhere to persist and users can't rename.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs</output>
